"text": "But a simulator is never quite the real world. Real joints have slack, floors aren't perfectly flat, and sensors are noisy. And Figure says this jump had to work at a foundry the team had never visited. A common fix is to make the simulation messy on purpose. Change the weight, the footing, the timing, a little every round, so the policy can't depend on one perfect world. We don't know which variations Figure used. It also rehearsed for real, with robots jumping from a second floor onto giant airbags. And the foundry did get messy. Figure says the heat and electromagnetic noise knocked out cameras and other electronics, and the policies kept running anyway.",
